    - Auto-repairing drift, syncing the host's wiring, upgrading anything, or otherwise mutating a file the user owns. The reporter is read-only; remediation flows through the user's visible command boundary.
    - Reporting installed files as outdated merely because a newer version is published when they match the version the project runs. Equally wrong is a pinned project behind latest told nothing, or told to install globally when it never chose that.
    - A version notice that floods the user with the full changelog or every entry of every skipped version. It is a short incentive to upgrade, not a release history.
